.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt VFS_LOOKUP 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_lookup
.Nd lookup a pathname in the virtual file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In vfs/vfs.h
.Ft fs_node_t *
.Fn vfs_lookup "fs_node_t *root" "const char *path"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vfs_lookup
function resolves a pathname to a VFS node
.Pq Vt fs_node_t ,
starting the search from the given
.Fa root
node.
.Pp
It transparently handles directory traversal, including crossing mount points and following symlinks (depending on internal implementation details).
.Pp
If
.Fa path
begins with '/', the leading slash is skipped, effectively treating it as relative to the provided
.Fa root .
Callers typically pass
.Va fs_root
as
.Fa root
for absolute paths.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn vfs_lookup
function returns a pointer to the found
.Vt fs_node_t
structure, or NULL if the path could not be resolved.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs 9 ,
.Xr vfs_mkdir 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn vfs_lookup
function appeared in Substrate.
